---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Page not found — Andrew Morrison"
  description="That page could not be found. It may have moved, been renamed, or never existed."
>
  <div class="content-container animate-in">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="section-label">404</span>
      <h1>This page has wandered off</h1>
      <div class="divider"></div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose about-prose">
      <p>
        The address you followed does not point at anything right now. Pages here get
        reorganised and renamed from time to time, so an old link may simply have moved.
        Nothing is broken on your end.
      </p>

      <p>Here are the reliable ways back in:</p>

      <ul class="notfound-links">
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog">Writing</a> (every post)</li>
        <li><a href="/projects">Projects</a> (ongoing work, grouped)</li>
        <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        If you reached this from a link on this site, I would like to fix it. The best place
        to flag it is <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrewnmorrison/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
.page-header { padding: 4rem 0 1rem; }
.page-header h1 { margin: 0.75rem 0; }
.about-prose { padding-bottom: 6rem; }

.notfound-links {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
}
.notfound-links li {
  padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem;
  border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
  background: var(--bg-surface);
  margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  font-size: 0.95rem;
}
.notfound-links li a { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 500; }
.notfound-links li a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
